slml 0.2
use"layout.slml"

@card{bg#fff p20 r12 b1 bc#e4e4ea g6}
@highlight{bg#fff4d6 bc#f0d48a}

doc{$title"Boxes and styles"
  t.lead"Every block element is a box. Its appearance is set with attributes, and sets of attributes you use often become *styles*."
  section{$id"box" $title"The box"
    c{g0
      ref{$name"p20" $values"number" $about"Padding: space inside the box on all sides."}
      ref{$name"px24  py8" $values"number" $about"Horizontal or vertical padding only; they override p."}
      ref{$name"bg#fff" $values"color" $about"Background color."}
      ref{$name"r12" $values"number" $about"Rounded corners."}
      ref{$name"b1  bc#ddd" $values"number, color" $about"Border width and color (light gray by default)."}
      ref{$name"sh:s  sh:l" $values"small, large" $about"A soft drop shadow."}
    }
    demo{$code"""
        c{bg#fff p20 r12 b1 bc#e4e4ea sh:s
          ###"A card"
          "Padding, fill, radius, border and shadow."
        }
        """
      c{bg#fff p20 r12 b1 bc#e4e4ea sh:s
        ###"A card"
        "Padding, fill, radius, border and shadow."
      }
    }
    note{$title"Sizes include padding and border"
      "A box with `w200 p20` is 200 pixels wide in total. There is no box-model arithmetic to remember."
    }
  }
  section{$id"styles" $title"Styles"
    "`@name{…}` gives a name to a set of attributes. Apply it with a dot after the element name. The element's own attributes win over the style's:"
    demo{$code"""
        @card{bg#fff p20 r12 b1 bc#e4e4ea g6}
        @highlight{bg#fff4d6 bc#f0d48a}

        r{g12
          c.card{w:f "Plain card"}
          c.card.highlight{w:f "Card + highlight"}
          c.card{w:f r0 "Square card"}
        }
        """
      r{g12
        c.card{w:f "Plain card"}
        c.card.highlight{w:f "Card + highlight"}
        c.card{w:f r0 "Square card"}
      }
    }
    -{g6
      "Styles are applied left to right, then the element's own attributes: `c.card.highlight{r0}`."
      "A style may only contain attributes that fit every element it is used on; `t.card` is an error here, because a text has no gap (`g`)."
      "Styles never cascade and have no selectors. An element looks the way its own line says."
      "Put styles you share between pages into a library file and `use` it. See [imports](/components.slml#imports)."
    }
  }
  section{$id"colors" $title"Colors"
    "Colors are hexadecimal: `#rgb`, `#rrggbb`, or with transparency `#rgba` / `#rrggbbaa`. There are no color names, so a color always means the same thing."
    r{g8 wrap
      t{bg#2457d6 c#fff p10 r8 "#2457d6"}
      t{bg#146c43 c#fff p10 r8 "#146c43"}
      t{bg#b42318 c#fff p10 r8 "#b42318"}
      t{bg#00000014 p10 r8 "#00000014"}
    }
  }
  pager{$prev"/layout-guide.slml" $prev-label"Layout" $next"/content.slml" $next-label"Lists, code and images"}
}
